 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "matching": "Judge the note as the person wrote it, before phone numbers are removed: the replacement token adds English-looking words that would hide a non-Latin note. Fold the note as the evidence pre-screen does (NFKD, drop combining marks, lowercase) and split on any code point that is not a letter or digit; drop words made only of digits. A word is non-Latin when it holds a letter outside a to z after folding. Count E, the words in `english`, and F, the words in `foreign` plus the non-Latin words. The note does NOT look English, and is refused for the cloud read, when more than half of its words are non-Latin, or when F is at least `minForeign` and F is more than `foreignOverEnglish` times E. Every other note, including one with no words, looks English.",
 "minForeign": 3,
 "foreignOverEnglish": 2,
 "source": "OURS: language screen before a cloud read. English notes quoting Spanish names or phrases pass; whole notes in Spanish, Portuguese, Vietnamese or Korean are refused. Known miss: a very short foreign note with few function words (for example \"Ella no esta aqui\") passes. Tuned on shared/test-vectors/language.json and on 325 English sentences from this repository's docs (0 refused).",
